---
import MotionPage from '@/components/MotionPage.astro';
import ForFramework from '@/components/ForFramework.astro';
import Code from '@/components/Code.astro';
import MotionStage from '@/components/motion/MotionStage.astro';
import MotionUsage from '@/components/motion/MotionUsage.astro';
import MotionOptions from '@/components/motion/MotionOptions.astro';
import MotionTokens from '@/components/motion/MotionTokens.astro';
import Svg from '@/components/motion/scenes/Svg.astro';
import { SvgControls } from '@/components/motion/scenes/SvgControls';
import { MotionSvgReact } from '@/examples/react/motion-svg.tsx';
import { MotionSvgAngular } from '@/examples/angular/motion-svg.ts';
import MotionSvgSvelte from '@/examples/svelte/motion-svg.svelte';
import { chipClass } from '@/components/motionDemo';

const defineCheck = `import { defineMotion } from '@udixio/motion';

// The check is drawn once, over the extra long curve, when it enters the view.
defineMotion('check-draw', {
  verb: 'reveal',
  keyframes: [{ draw: 0 }, { draw: 1 }],
  timing: { duration: 'duration.extraLong1', easing: 'easing.standard' },
});`;

const defineTravel = `import { defineMotion } from '@udixio/motion';

// The dot starts at the start of its offset path, and travels to its end when it enters the view.
defineMotion('travel', {
  verb: 'reveal',
  keyframes: [{ along: 0 }, { along: 1 }],
  timing: { duration: 'duration.extraLong2', easing: 'easing.standard' },
});`;

const morphIcon = `import { morph } from '@udixio/motion/svg';

// The icon takes the shape of a pause bar. The handle ends when the shape is there.
const icon = document.querySelector<SVGPathElement>('#icon')!;
const handle = morph(icon, 'M7 5 H10 V19 H7 Z M14 5 H17 V19 H14 Z');
const result = await handle.finished; // 'finished', or 'cancelled' when cancel() stopped it`;
---
<MotionPage
  slug="svg"
  title="Motion: draw or morph SVG"
  description="Draw a stroke, move an element along a path, and morph one path into another, in HTML, React, Angular and Svelte."
  frameworkSwitch
>
  <ForFramework as="span" slot="summary">
    <Fragment slot="html">Put <code>data-motion</code> on a path or a shape: it draws, or travels along its path. <code>morph()</code> reshapes a path into another.</Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="react">Render a path with <code>useMotion</code>: <code>play()</code> replays its draw or its travel. <code>morph()</code> reshapes a path into another.</Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="angular">Put <code>udxMotion</code> on a path or a shape: its <code>play()</code> replays its draw or its travel. <code>morph()</code> reshapes a path into another.</Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="svelte">Attach <code>motion()</code> to a path or a shape: <code>play()</code> on its binding replays its draw or its travel. <code>morph()</code> reshapes a path into another.</Fragment>
  </ForFramework>

  <MotionStage scene="svg" label="Live example: Draw or morph SVG" height={360}>
    <Fragment slot="controls"><SvgControls client:visible size="page" /></Fragment>
    <Svg size="page" />
    <Fragment slot="readout"><span class={`${chipClass} tracking-normal`} data-svg-readout>morph: 'Cookie'</span></Fragment>
  </MotionStage>

  <h2>Draw a stroke</h2>
  <p>
    <code>draw</code>, from 0 to 1, draws a path or a basic shape from nothing to its whole stroke. A finished draw gives the
    stroke back to the stylesheet at rest, and a binding gives it back when it is destroyed. The preset <code>draw</code> is an
    <code>appear</code> that draws the shape from nothing to its whole stroke as it enters.
  </p>
  <Code data-code={defineCheck} data-language="ts" />
  <ForFramework>
    <Fragment slot="html">
      <p>Put <code>data-motion="check-draw"</code> on the path, and call <code>connectMotion()</code> once for the page.</p>
    </Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="react">
      <p>Call <code>useMotion&lt;SVGPathElement&gt;('check-draw')</code>, put its <code>ref</code> on the path, and call <code>play()</code> to draw it again.</p>
    </Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="angular">
      <p>Add <code>Motion</code> to your component's <code>imports</code>, and put <code>udxMotion="check-draw"</code> on the path. To draw it again, take the directive in a template reference, and call its <code>play()</code>.</p>
    </Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="svelte">
      <p>Attach the path with <code>&#123;&#64;attach motion('check-draw')&#125;</code>. To draw it again, take the path with <code>bind:this</code>, and call <code>getMotion(path, 'view')?.play()</code>, from <code>@udixio/motion</code>.</p>
    </Fragment>
  </ForFramework>

  <h2>Move an element along a path</h2>
  <p>
    <code>along</code>, from 0 to 1, moves an element along the <code>offset-path</code> its CSS gives it, by writing
    <code>offset-distance</code>. An element that is out of view when the page connects starts at the beginning of its path.
    An element that is in view keeps the <code>offset-distance</code> its stylesheet gives it, so set <code>offset-distance: 100%</code>
    there for a travel that rests at its end.
  </p>
  <Code data-code={defineTravel} data-language="ts" />

  <h2>Morph one shape into another</h2>
  <p>
    <code>morph(path, to, &#123; timing, precision &#125;)</code>, from <code>@udixio/motion/svg</code>, morphs the <code>d</code>
    of a path into the <code>d</code> of another path, or into a <code>d</code> string. Both shapes are resampled, so they need
    not have the same number of points. <code>morph</code> draws with anime.js, a dependency of <code>@udixio/motion</code>, so
    the package installs it for you.
  </p>
  <Code data-code={morphIcon} data-language="ts" />
  <p>
    The path must be inside an SVG. Call <code>cancel()</code> on the handle to stop the morph where the shape is: a new morph
    continues from that shape. When the morph ends, the path carries exactly the <code>d</code> of the target.
  </p>
  <ForFramework>
    <p slot="html">Take the path with <code>getElementById</code>, and call <code>morph()</code> from the click listener of the button.</p>
    <p slot="react">Keep the path in a <code>ref</code>, and call <code>morph()</code> from a handler.</p>
    <p slot="angular">Read the path with <code>@ViewChild</code>, and call <code>morph()</code> from a method.</p>
    <p slot="svelte">Take the path with <code>bind:this</code>, and call <code>morph()</code> from a function.</p>
  </ForFramework>

  <h2>Use it in the frameworks</h2>
  <p>
    The live example draws the check once, when it enters the view. Draw again draws it from nothing, and Move again travels the
    dot along its path. The icon morphs between play and pause, and a new morph continues from the shape the icon has reached.
  </p>
  <MotionUsage name="motion-svg" previewHeight={[480, 456]}>
    <MotionSvgReact slot="react" client:visible />
    <MotionSvgAngular slot="angular" client:visible />
    <MotionSvgSvelte slot="svelte" client:visible />
  </MotionUsage>

  <h2>Options</h2>
  <p><code>draw</code> and <code>along</code> are keyframe fields, not options: a definition writes them in its keyframes, as above. <code>morph</code> takes these two options.</p>
  <MotionOptions
    rows={[
      { name: 'timing', values: 'spring.* token, or a curve', default: 'spring.default.spatial', description: 'The timing of the morph. A spring falls back to its curve on anime.js.' },
      { name: 'precision', values: 'a number of points per unit of length', description: 'How finely the two shapes are resampled. 0 morphs the two strings as they are.' },
    ]}
  />

  <h2>Timing and tokens</h2>
  <p>A morph moves on the default spatial spring unless <code>timing</code> names another. The check and the dot are drawn over the extra long curves of their definitions.</p>
  <MotionTokens tokens={['spring.default.spatial', 'duration.extraLong1', 'duration.extraLong2', 'easing.standard']} />

  <h2>Reduced motion</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Under reduced motion, an entry that draws sets its stroke at once, and an <code>along</code> entry moves at once.</li>
    <li>An exit keeps the stroke it has, or the place it is at, and fades: nothing is redrawn or moved under reduced motion.</li>
    <li><code>morph</code> sets the shape at once under reduced motion, with <code>--udx-motion: none</code>, or with a zero motion scale.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Limits</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>If you need a layout motion on an element, use an HTML element: a layout motion throws on an SVG element.</li>
    <li>If two motions draw the same shape at once, they share its dash, and the last one written stays. Draw each stroke with its own path.</li>
    <li>If a value, a sequence or a gesture must follow a graphic, bind it to an HTML element around the SVG: those bind to HTML elements only.</li>
  </ul>
</MotionPage>
